WEBVTT

1
00:00:16.257 --> 00:00:22.361
Two months later, after the robbery at the bishop's home, a stranger entered a small French city at

2
00:00:22.401 --> 00:00:27.025
dusk. Carrying a knapsack and a walking stick, he looked like a laborer.

3
00:00:28.065 --> 00:00:31.688
Just as he arrived in the city, a fire broke out in the city hall.

4
00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:37.885
The man rushed into the building and risked his life to save two children—the police chief's children.

5
00:00:38.706 --> 00:00:44.711
The stranger did not show his yellow identity card, and in the confusion surrounding the fire, no one

6
00:00:44.791 --> 00:00:45.511
asked him for it.

7
00:00:46.592 --> 00:00:51.356
And that is how Jean Valjean started a new life in a new city with a new name:

8
00:00:51.837 --> 00:00:52.958
Monsieur Madeleine.

9
00:00:53.878 --> 00:00:58.883
The city had once been famous for a special kind of black jewelry, but the jewelry industry had

10
00:00:58.963 --> 00:01:00.204
fallen on hard times.

11
00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:04.882
Madeleine, however, soon discovered a way to make the jewelry more cheaply.

12
00:01:05.703 --> 00:01:08.705
Everyone benefited from this new manufacturing process.

13
00:01:09.485 --> 00:01:14.708
The factories made more money; the factory workers' wages went up, and consumers paid less.

14
00:01:16.269 --> 00:01:21.312
As for Madeleine, he built a large factory with separate workshops for men and women.

15
00:01:21.992 --> 00:01:26.115
He required that all his employees be honest and of good moral character.

16
00:01:26.915 --> 00:01:33.300
By 1820 he had made a fortune and deposited more than 600,000 francs in the bank.

17
00:01:33.901 --> 00:01:38.765
But before doing that, he spent more than a million francs on the city and its poor.

18
00:01:39.546 --> 00:01:46.292
He improved the hospital and replaced the miserable schoolhouse with two new schools, one for boys and one

19
00:01:46.352 --> 00:01:46.872
for girls.

20
00:01:47.813 --> 00:01:53.798
People begged him to become the mayor, but Madeleine refused, and nothing could persuade him to change his

21
00:01:53.858 --> 00:01:59.077
mind. Then one day an old woman called out to him as he passed her doorstep.

22
00:01:59.097 --> 00:02:01.778
"A good mayor is a good thing.

23
00:02:02.339 --> 00:02:04.299
Are you afraid of the good you can do?"

24
00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:09.361
Her words struck him, and soon he was Mayor Madeleine.

25
00:02:09.942 --> 00:02:12.102
Nevertheless he continued to live simply.

26
00:02:13.023 --> 00:02:17.184
He fulfilled his duties as mayor but led an isolated life beyond that.

27
00:02:18.665 --> 00:02:23.787
Although he was no longer young, he was still very strong and was always willing to lend a

28
00:02:23.827 --> 00:02:25.628
hand to anyone who needed help.

29
00:02:26.516 --> 00:02:32.880
Whenever he went out, his pockets were full of money, but when he returned, they were empty because

30
00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:34.360
he had given it all away.

31
00:02:35.341 --> 00:02:40.184
The mayor was especially kind to chimney sweeps, who passed through the city looking for work.

32
00:02:40.764 --> 00:02:42.965
He always asked their names and handed them money.

33
00:02:43.846 --> 00:02:48.188
Mayor Madeleine was a pleasant man, but there was something sad about him.

34
00:02:49.069 --> 00:02:54.132
People saw him as a rich man who was not proud, a fortunate man who did not appear

35
00:02:54.192 --> 00:03:00.923
content. At the beginning of 1821, the local newspaper reported the death of Bishop Myriel.

36
00:03:01.804 --> 00:03:05.326
The next morning when the mayor went out, he was dressed all in black.

37
00:03:06.006 --> 00:03:08.948
Everyone wondered why he was mourning the death of the bishop.

38
00:03:08.968 --> 00:03:13.790
"You must be a relative of the bishop's," one elderly woman said to him.

39
00:03:13.810 --> 00:03:17.632
"No, madame," he replied respectfully.

40
00:03:17.652 --> 00:03:20.434
"Then why do you wear mourning for him?"

41
00:03:20.454 --> 00:03:23.976
"In my youth I was a servant for his family."

42
00:03:25.497 --> 00:03:30.280
"Ah!" The woman seemed satisfied with his explanation and no one else questioned him.

43
00:03:31.080 --> 00:03:34.303
Time passed and everyone grew to respect the mayor.

44
00:03:34.903 --> 00:03:37.625
People came from thirty miles around to consult him.

45
00:03:38.526 --> 00:03:43.349
Mayor Madeleine settled differences, prevented lawsuits, and reconciled enemies.

46
00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:49.073
He seemed to have a sense of what was good and fair, a natural understanding of the law.

47
00:03:49.994 --> 00:03:56.021
There was, however, one man who held himself apart and refused to be drawn into admiring the mayor.

48
00:03:57.021 --> 00:04:00.922
His name was Javert, and he was an inspector in the police department.

49
00:04:01.802 --> 00:04:08.104
Often when the mayor passed along the street, acknowledging the greetings of his followers, Javert stood alone, watching

50
00:04:08.164 --> 00:04:13.746
him. "I know I've seen that man somewhere before," Javert said to himself.

51
00:04:13.766 --> 00:04:14.966
"But where?"

52
00:04:15.826 --> 00:04:17.607
Javert had been born in a prison.

53
00:04:18.107 --> 00:04:22.448
His mother was a fortune-teller and his father was a convict on a prison ship.

54
00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:26.661
In his youth Javert worked as a guard on a prison ship.

55
00:04:27.262 --> 00:04:33.084
He had great respect for authority, but he had nothing but disgust for anyone who broke the law.

56
00:04:34.024 --> 00:04:37.006
Harsh and judgmental, he made no exceptions.

57
00:04:37.646 --> 00:04:40.967
Javert would have arrested his own father for escaping from prison.

58
00:04:41.548 --> 00:04:45.649
Javert's role in life was to be a spy and an informer.

59
00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:51.712
Javert always kept an eye on Madeleine, an eye full of suspicion and speculation.

60
00:04:52.660 --> 00:04:57.502
The mayor endured this unpleasant and annoying stare without appearing to pay any attention to it.

61
00:04:58.323 --> 00:05:02.644
He treated Javert as he treated everyone else—with kindness and a friendly manner.

62
00:05:03.565 --> 00:05:08.727
One morning the mayor was walking along one of the back alleys when he heard shouting and saw

63
00:05:08.767 --> 00:05:09.707
a crowd gathering.

64
00:05:11.108 --> 00:05:13.849
A horse had been pulling a cart when it stumbled and fell.

65
00:05:14.329 --> 00:05:20.252
In trying to help the horse, its owner—an old man named Fauchelevent—had fallen under the cart.

66
00:05:21.140 --> 00:05:24.361
The cart was heavily loaded so there was no way to pull the man out.

67
00:05:24.381 --> 00:05:27.022
"Help!" cried Fauchelevent.

68
00:05:27.042 --> 00:05:28.842
"I'm being crushed to death!"

69
00:05:29.842 --> 00:05:32.003
Mayor Madeleine approached and the crowd parted.

70
00:05:32.503 --> 00:05:37.184
He quickly saw that the only way to free the old man was to lift the cart.

71
00:05:37.204 --> 00:05:39.265
"Does anybody have a jack?"

72
00:05:39.565 --> 00:05:40.085
he asked.

73
00:05:40.745 --> 00:05:43.406
"Someone has gone to fetch one," replied a peasant.

74
00:05:43.426 --> 00:05:45.447
"How soon will it be here?"

75
00:05:45.467 --> 00:05:49.668
"The jack is at the blacksmith's, but it will take at least a quarter of an hour to

76
00:05:49.728 --> 00:05:51.985
arrive." "Fifteen minutes!"

77
00:05:52.465 --> 00:05:55.407
exclaimed the mayor as he watched the cart's wheels sinking in the mud.

78
00:05:55.427 --> 00:05:57.028
"We can't wait that long."

79
00:05:57.048 --> 00:06:00.691
"It can't be helped," said someone else in the crowd.

80
00:06:00.711 --> 00:06:06.955
"Listen," said Madeleine, "there's still room enough for a man to crawl under the wagon and lift it

81
00:06:06.995 --> 00:06:07.555
with his back.

82
00:06:08.456 --> 00:06:10.337
In half a minute, we'll have the poor man out.

83
00:06:10.937 --> 00:06:13.459
Is there no one who has the strength and courage to do it?

84
00:06:13.899 --> 00:06:15.600
I'll give him five gold coins."

85
00:06:16.661 --> 00:06:18.162
No one stirred in the crowd.

86
00:06:18.683 --> 00:06:19.683
"Ten gold coins!"

87
00:06:20.043 --> 00:06:20.584
said the mayor.

88
00:06:21.068 --> 00:06:22.569
The bystanders dropped their eyes.

89
00:06:23.570 --> 00:06:28.173
One of them muttered, "A man would have to be awfully strong, and even then he'd risk getting

90
00:06:28.213 --> 00:06:31.175
crushed." "Come, someone, anyone!"

91
00:06:31.535 --> 00:06:32.236
said Madeleine.

92
00:06:32.756 --> 00:06:34.097
"Twenty gold coins."

93
00:06:35.158 --> 00:06:36.239
The same silence.

94
00:06:36.999 --> 00:06:39.161
"It's not that they aren't willing," said a voice.

95
00:06:40.121 --> 00:06:43.364
The mayor spun around and saw Javert, who continued to speak.

96
00:06:43.384 --> 00:06:45.405
"But they don't have the strength.

97
00:06:46.046 --> 00:06:49.328
You'd need a terribly strong man to raise a cart like that on his back."

98
00:06:50.740 --> 00:06:55.222
Then Javert looked the mayor in the eye and said, "I've known only one man capable of doing

99
00:06:55.263 --> 00:06:57.304
that." Madeleine shuddered.

100
00:06:57.324 --> 00:06:59.905
"He was a convict on the prison ships at Toulon."

101
00:07:00.245 --> 00:07:03.927
Javert said this casually, but he never took his eyes off the mayor.

102
00:07:04.928 --> 00:07:06.308
Madeleine turned pale.

103
00:07:06.929 --> 00:07:09.270
Meanwhile the cart continued to sink in the mud.

104
00:07:09.290 --> 00:07:11.211
"I'm dying!"

105
00:07:11.711 --> 00:07:12.672
screamed Fauchelevent.

106
00:07:13.312 --> 00:07:14.693
"Will no one help me?"

107
00:07:15.733 --> 00:07:21.305
With Javert's eyes still on him, the mayor looked at the peasants who stood there watching, and smiled

108
00:07:21.385 --> 00:07:27.230
sadly. Then he fell on his knees and before the crowd could stop him, he was under the

109
00:07:27.270 --> 00:07:32.575
cart. There was an awful moment of silence as the mayor tried in vain to lift the cart.

110
00:07:33.416 --> 00:07:35.738
Then the victim himself called out a warning.

111
00:07:35.758 --> 00:07:38.060
"Stop!" cried Fauchelevent.

112
00:07:38.080 --> 00:07:40.583
"Or you will be crushed to death with me!"
